INSERT INTO sat_questions (question_id, external_id, vault_id, disclosed_item_id, source, program, test_type, test_type_desc, domain, primary_class_cd, skill_cd, skill_desc, difficulty, score_band_range_cd, question_type, stimulus_html, stem_html, answer_options, correct_answer, answer_keys, rationale_html, correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale, image_count, parent_template_name, parent_template_id, template_cluster_id, template_cluster_name, origin, position, answer_style, section, raw_payload, created_date, updated_date) VALUES
    ($SATQ$db3ad406$SATQ$, $SATQ$3be7c190-7615-4bc8-b801-6780fee56ba0$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$f0c76abd-3410-4438-929b-e5ace14ddfcc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Stars form in a galaxy when gravity causes a massive cloud of dust and gas to collapse.</li>
<li>A galaxy in a phase of rapid star formation is called a starburst galaxy.</li>
<li>Quenching is a process in which a galaxy loses star-forming gas.</li>
<li>A galaxy that no longer forms stars is called a quenched galaxy.</li>
<li>A quenched galaxy has entered the poststarburst phase.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to explain what a quenched galaxy is. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"546a39da-ae87-45ef-931a-a71d8b7f3e36","content":"<p>Before quenching, a starburst galaxy will form stars at a rapid rate.</p>"},{"id":"8c815e0b-6d76-4440-a61d-fde89b457f09","content":"<p>When it becomes quenched, a starburst galaxy enters the poststarburst phase.</p>"},{"id":"c3474381-12bb-4eed-995a-75234c13145a","content":"<p>Having entered the poststarburst phase, a quenched galaxy is one that no longer forms stars.</p>"},{"id":"c5a5e9b3-d39c-4a0a-b757-17bfeec97220","content":"<p>A starburst galaxy will lose star-forming gas and eventually become quenched.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c3474381-12bb-4eed-995a-75234c13145a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. This choice defines a quenched galaxy as &ldquo;one that no longer forms stars.&rdquo; </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice only describes what happens before quenching. Choice B is incorrect. This choice only describes what happens after quenching. Choice D is incorrect. This choice only describes what causes quenching. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-H009$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$44391890-17bb-4e89-83a6-151691589e9b$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"db3ad406","external_id":"3be7c190-7615-4bc8-b801-6780fee56ba0","vaultid":"f0c76abd-3410-4438-929b-e5ace14ddfcc","uId":"a857a7b9-10c9-42dc-a255-df913637095f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stars form in a galaxy when gravity causes a massive cloud of dust and gas to collapse.</li>\n<li>A galaxy in a phase of rapid star formation is called a starburst galaxy.</li>\n<li>Quenching is a process in which a galaxy loses star-forming gas.</li>\n<li>A galaxy that no longer forms stars is called a quenched galaxy.</li>\n<li>A quenched galaxy has entered the poststarburst phase.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to explain what a quenched galaxy is. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"546a39da-ae87-45ef-931a-a71d8b7f3e36","content":"<p>Before quenching, a starburst galaxy will form stars at a rapid rate.</p>"},{"id":"8c815e0b-6d76-4440-a61d-fde89b457f09","content":"<p>When it becomes quenched, a starburst galaxy enters the poststarburst phase.</p>"},{"id":"c3474381-12bb-4eed-995a-75234c13145a","content":"<p>Having entered the poststarburst phase, a quenched galaxy is one that no longer forms stars.</p>"},{"id":"c5a5e9b3-d39c-4a0a-b757-17bfeec97220","content":"<p>A starburst galaxy will lose star-forming gas and eventually become quenched.</p>"}],"keys":["c3474381-12bb-4eed-995a-75234c13145a"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. This choice defines a quenched galaxy as &ldquo;one that no longer forms stars.&rdquo; </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice only describes what happens before quenching. Choice B is incorrect. This choice only describes what happens after quenching. Choice D is incorrect. This choice only describes what causes quenching. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-H009","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"44391890-17bb-4e89-83a6-151691589e9b","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959372,"updateDate":1691007959372}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959372, 1691007959372),
    ($SATQ$db8fe023$SATQ$, $SATQ$5c009062-358e-46dd-9192-afa0812947b8$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$772b7b12-2ef1-4ce3-be90-1ab51dd1a30c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>A potter choosing which type of clay to use for a piece considers two key factors: the desired look of the piece and its intended use. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> earthenware clay is often used for decorative pieces because of its rustic look. This type of clay is not often used in industrial settings, though, because it is less durable than other clays.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b2fbb232-5bc8-47cc-a703-8f9a9bb75a9f","content":"<p>In other words,</p>"},{"id":"88a7eac0-15c3-4aa0-a3f6-105b083439ef","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"},{"id":"037dd8bd-ba0c-4980-a751-bf2442b847d3","content":"<p>In conclusion,</p>"},{"id":"8e3861ec-f413-4715-aef6-76513a02bfb6","content":"<p>For example,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8e3861ec-f413-4715-aef6-76513a02bfb6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The previous sentence tells us that potters think about the look and use of a piece when selecting clay. This sentence provides a specific example of a type of clay selected for its appearance, so the transition "for example" fits perfectly.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates a restatement of the same idea. But this sentence does more than just restate the previous idea. Instead, it provides a more specific example of the idea presented in the first sentence. Choice B is incorrect. This choice uses a disagreement transition. But this sentence actually agrees with the previous sentence. Both sentences suggest that desired look plays a role in the selection of clay types for pottery pieces. Choice C is incorrect. This choice uses a concluding transition. But this sentence doesn&rsquo;t sum up the previous sentence. Instead, it gives a specific example of the idea presented in the previous sentence.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TRA-E006$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$beb607bc-f445-4363-99d3-42faa4a0e647$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"db8fe023","external_id":"5c009062-358e-46dd-9192-afa0812947b8","vaultid":"772b7b12-2ef1-4ce3-be90-1ab51dd1a30c","uId":"250839e6-d018-4f9c-9a85-2db5122ae572","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>A potter choosing which type of clay to use for a piece considers two key factors: the desired look of the piece and its intended use. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> earthenware clay is often used for decorative pieces because of its rustic look. This type of clay is not often used in industrial settings, though, because it is less durable than other clays.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b2fbb232-5bc8-47cc-a703-8f9a9bb75a9f","content":"<p>In other words,</p>"},{"id":"88a7eac0-15c3-4aa0-a3f6-105b083439ef","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"},{"id":"037dd8bd-ba0c-4980-a751-bf2442b847d3","content":"<p>In conclusion,</p>"},{"id":"8e3861ec-f413-4715-aef6-76513a02bfb6","content":"<p>For example,</p>"}],"keys":["8e3861ec-f413-4715-aef6-76513a02bfb6"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The previous sentence tells us that potters think about the look and use of a piece when selecting clay. This sentence provides a specific example of a type of clay selected for its appearance, so the transition \"for example\" fits perfectly.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This choice uses a transition that indicates a restatement of the same idea. But this sentence does more than just restate the previous idea. Instead, it provides a more specific example of the idea presented in the first sentence. Choice B is incorrect. This choice uses a disagreement transition. But this sentence actually agrees with the previous sentence. Both sentences suggest that desired look plays a role in the selection of clay types for pottery pieces. Choice C is incorrect. This choice uses a concluding transition. But this sentence doesn&rsquo;t sum up the previous sentence. Instead, it gives a specific example of the idea presented in the previous sentence.</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TRA-E006","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"beb607bc-f445-4363-99d3-42faa4a0e647","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959373,"updateDate":1691007959373}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959373, 1691007959373),
    ($SATQ$dd087f31$SATQ$, $SATQ$87521ec5-ad3e-4d1c-9e34-101e74b235b9$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$e5e3e83b-aa5f-40e7-8323-aeff3228ab19$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie&rsquo;s 2013 novel <em>Americanah</em> chronicles the divergent experiences of Ifemelu and Obinze, a young Nigerian couple, after high school. Ifemelu moves to the United States to attend a prestigious university. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> Obinze travels to London, hoping to start a career there. However, frustrated with the lack of opportunities, he soon returns to Nigeria.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ca77298f-72ce-407d-a2da-8ff2f4126573","content":"<p>Meanwhile,</p>"},{"id":"e287aff5-977f-454a-b7b8-bf0433ef039e","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"fd433526-8fc3-491f-aa94-436d78d12d91","content":"<p>Secondly,</p>"},{"id":"81ffb764-f5e0-4740-8e53-e90c16801968","content":"<p>In fact,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ca77298f-72ce-407d-a2da-8ff2f4126573"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. &ldquo;Meanwhile&rdquo; logically signals that the action described in this sentence (Obinze&rsquo;s move to London to pursue a career) is simultaneous with the action described in the previous sentence (Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States). The first sentence establishes that the actions take place around the same time, referring to the characters&rsquo; &ldquo;divergent experiences&rdquo; following high school. &nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;nevertheless&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about Obinze&rsquo;s move to London is true despite the previous information about Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States. Instead, as the first sentence establishes, Obinze&rsquo;s move and Ifemelu&rsquo;s move are related, parallel experiences that occur around the same time.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;secondly&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a second point or reason separate from the previous information about Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States. Instead, as the first sentence establishes, Obinze&rsquo;s move and Ifemelu&rsquo;s move are related, parallel experiences that occur around the same time.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;in fact&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence emphasizes, modifies, or contradicts the previous information about Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States. Instead, as the first sentence establishes, Obinze&rsquo;s move and Ifemelu&rsquo;s move are related, parallel experiences that occur around the same time.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-240-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$e24dd4bc-33c8-426c-ae60-6b72999d32f8$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"dd087f31","external_id":"87521ec5-ad3e-4d1c-9e34-101e74b235b9","vaultid":"e5e3e83b-aa5f-40e7-8323-aeff3228ab19","uId":"9d73f9dc-42e1-4849-8012-8a9306fa8d6b","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Chimamanda Ngozi Adichie&rsquo;s 2013 novel <em>Americanah</em> chronicles the divergent experiences of Ifemelu and Obinze, a young Nigerian couple, after high school. Ifemelu moves to the United States to attend a prestigious university. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> Obinze travels to London, hoping to start a career there. However, frustrated with the lack of opportunities, he soon returns to Nigeria.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ca77298f-72ce-407d-a2da-8ff2f4126573","content":"<p>Meanwhile,</p>"},{"id":"e287aff5-977f-454a-b7b8-bf0433ef039e","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"fd433526-8fc3-491f-aa94-436d78d12d91","content":"<p>Secondly,</p>"},{"id":"81ffb764-f5e0-4740-8e53-e90c16801968","content":"<p>In fact,</p>"}],"keys":["ca77298f-72ce-407d-a2da-8ff2f4126573"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. &ldquo;Meanwhile&rdquo; logically signals that the action described in this sentence (Obinze&rsquo;s move to London to pursue a career) is simultaneous with the action described in the previous sentence (Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States). The first sentence establishes that the actions take place around the same time, referring to the characters&rsquo; &ldquo;divergent experiences&rdquo; following high school. &nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;nevertheless&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about Obinze&rsquo;s move to London is true despite the previous information about Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States. Instead, as the first sentence establishes, Obinze&rsquo;s move and Ifemelu&rsquo;s move are related, parallel experiences that occur around the same time.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;secondly&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is a second point or reason separate from the previous information about Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States. Instead, as the first sentence establishes, Obinze&rsquo;s move and Ifemelu&rsquo;s move are related, parallel experiences that occur around the same time.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;in fact&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence emphasizes, modifies, or contradicts the previous information about Ifemelu&rsquo;s move to the United States. Instead, as the first sentence establishes, Obinze&rsquo;s move and Ifemelu&rsquo;s move are related, parallel experiences that occur around the same time.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-240-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"e24dd4bc-33c8-426c-ae60-6b72999d32f8","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959333,"updateDate":1691007959333}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959333, 1691007959333),
    ($SATQ$dd11e5ab$SATQ$, $SATQ$bdfb2b51-a55e-4114-a6fe-e6b6206c8b3c$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$b548dd55-1b50-460b-bbbe-cbfac76766e0$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Muckrakers were journalists who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era (1897&ndash;1920).</li>
<li>Ida Tarbell was a muckraker who investigated the Standard Oil Company.</li>
<li>She interviewed Standard Oil Company executives, oil industry workers, and public officials.</li>
<li>She examined thousands of pages of the company&rsquo;s internal communications, including letters and financial records.</li>
<li>Her book <em>The History of the Standard Oil Company</em> (1904) exposed the company&rsquo;s unfair business practices.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize the thoroughness of Ida Tarbell&rsquo;s investigation of the Standard Oil Company. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"7d2e0b87-5230-4b86-b2a7-370fbd4cb6a1","content":"<p>Ida Tarbell not only interviewed Standard Oil executives, oil industry workers, and public officials but also examined thousands of pages of the company&rsquo;s internal communications.</p>"},{"id":"067724e7-11f6-4a5b-bd6e-70836824ac88","content":"<p>Ida Tarbell, who investigated the Standard Oil Company, was a muckraker (a journalist who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era, 1897&ndash;1920).</p>"},{"id":"7a95cc11-5e02-4067-9ee5-bfd4ea6adbe1","content":"<p>As part of her investigation of the Standard Oil Company, muckraker Ida Tarbell conducted interviews.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"37e96ca8-dfca-4d4e-9651-5540537d50a6","content":"<p>Published in 1904, muckraker Ida Tarbell&rsquo;s book <em>The History of the Standard Oil Company</em> exposed the company&rsquo;s unfair business practices.&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["7d2e0b87-5230-4b86-b2a7-370fbd4cb6a1"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. It describes Tarbell&rsquo;s investigation and the lengths she went to complete it. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe how thorough Tarbell was. Instead, it gives a biographical sketch. Choice C is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe how thorough Tarbell was. Tarbell didn&rsquo;t only conduct interviews&mdash;she also &ldquo;examined thousands of pages of the company&rsquo;s internal communications.&rdquo; Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe how thorough Tarbell was. It describes her book but doesn&rsquo;t include anything about her investigation. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-M004$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$c04b2dec-1413-433f-af6d-8d08dd3b2fa0$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"dd11e5ab","external_id":"bdfb2b51-a55e-4114-a6fe-e6b6206c8b3c","vaultid":"b548dd55-1b50-460b-bbbe-cbfac76766e0","uId":"3520b078-2ad3-45a0-b67c-a6b665168a6f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Muckrakers were journalists who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era (1897&ndash;1920).</li>\n<li>Ida Tarbell was a muckraker who investigated the Standard Oil Company.</li>\n<li>She interviewed Standard Oil Company executives, oil industry workers, and public officials.</li>\n<li>She examined thousands of pages of the company&rsquo;s internal communications, including letters and financial records.</li>\n<li>Her book <em>The History of the Standard Oil Company</em> (1904) exposed the company&rsquo;s unfair business practices.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize the thoroughness of Ida Tarbell&rsquo;s investigation of the Standard Oil Company. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"7d2e0b87-5230-4b86-b2a7-370fbd4cb6a1","content":"<p>Ida Tarbell not only interviewed Standard Oil executives, oil industry workers, and public officials but also examined thousands of pages of the company&rsquo;s internal communications.</p>"},{"id":"067724e7-11f6-4a5b-bd6e-70836824ac88","content":"<p>Ida Tarbell, who investigated the Standard Oil Company, was a muckraker (a journalist who sought to expose corruption in US institutions during the Progressive Era, 1897&ndash;1920).</p>"},{"id":"7a95cc11-5e02-4067-9ee5-bfd4ea6adbe1","content":"<p>As part of her investigation of the Standard Oil Company, muckraker Ida Tarbell conducted interviews.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"37e96ca8-dfca-4d4e-9651-5540537d50a6","content":"<p>Published in 1904, muckraker Ida Tarbell&rsquo;s book <em>The History of the Standard Oil Company</em> exposed the company&rsquo;s unfair business practices.&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["7d2e0b87-5230-4b86-b2a7-370fbd4cb6a1"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. It describes Tarbell&rsquo;s investigation and the lengths she went to complete it. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe how thorough Tarbell was. Instead, it gives a biographical sketch. Choice C is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe how thorough Tarbell was. Tarbell didn&rsquo;t only conduct interviews&mdash;she also &ldquo;examined thousands of pages of the company&rsquo;s internal communications.&rdquo; Choice D is incorrect. This choice doesn&rsquo;t describe how thorough Tarbell was. It describes her book but doesn&rsquo;t include anything about her investigation. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-M004","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"c04b2dec-1413-433f-af6d-8d08dd3b2fa0","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959372,"updateDate":1691007959372}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959372, 1691007959372),
    ($SATQ$ddb77846$SATQ$, $SATQ$61e4987d-fb06-4147-acf3-d01a7f3b36f2$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>My interest in old public libraries has led me to seek them out whenever I visit a new part of the United States. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> I could visit every state in the US and still not find the oldest public library in the Western Hemisphere. That library, the Biblioteca Palafoxiana, is located in Puebla, Mexico.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d54914c0-08e5-4143-a347-28dd7ee86269","content":"<p>As a result,</p>"},{"id":"165b9b68-34db-437e-bce1-e209c21bd348","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"901698c2-2443-4ae4-a9ec-5c2e5a452364","content":"<p>Earlier,</p>"},{"id":"d5818a5a-8ef5-4446-a660-f77c64e4d8d2","content":"<p>In other words,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["165b9b68-34db-437e-bce1-e209c21bd348"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. "Nevertheless" logically signals that the claim in the sentence&mdash;that the speaker could visit every state in the US and not find the oldest public library in the Western Hemisphere&mdash;is true despite the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "as a result" illogically signals that the claim in the sentence is a consequence of the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries. Instead, the claim is true despite the previous claim. Choice C is incorrect because "earlier" illogically signals that the claim in the sentence occurs earlier in a chronological sequence of events than the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries. Instead, the claim is true despite the previous claim. Choice D is incorrect because "in other words" illogically signals that the claim in the sentence is merely a paraphrase or restatement of the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries. Instead, the claim is true despite the previous claim.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ddb77846","external_id":"61e4987d-fb06-4147-acf3-d01a7f3b36f2","vaultid":null,"uId":"5979bfe7-6644-43f4-a4e4-58fa1f365aa4","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>My interest in old public libraries has led me to seek them out whenever I visit a new part of the United States. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> I could visit every state in the US and still not find the oldest public library in the Western Hemisphere. That library, the Biblioteca Palafoxiana, is located in Puebla, Mexico.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d54914c0-08e5-4143-a347-28dd7ee86269","content":"<p>As a result,</p>"},{"id":"165b9b68-34db-437e-bce1-e209c21bd348","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"901698c2-2443-4ae4-a9ec-5c2e5a452364","content":"<p>Earlier,</p>"},{"id":"d5818a5a-8ef5-4446-a660-f77c64e4d8d2","content":"<p>In other words,</p>"}],"keys":["165b9b68-34db-437e-bce1-e209c21bd348"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. \"Nevertheless\" logically signals that the claim in the sentence&mdash;that the speaker could visit every state in the US and not find the oldest public library in the Western Hemisphere&mdash;is true despite the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"as a result\" illogically signals that the claim in the sentence is a consequence of the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries. Instead, the claim is true despite the previous claim. Choice C is incorrect because \"earlier\" illogically signals that the claim in the sentence occurs earlier in a chronological sequence of events than the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries. Instead, the claim is true despite the previous claim. Choice D is incorrect because \"in other words\" illogically signals that the claim in the sentence is merely a paraphrase or restatement of the previous claim about the speaker seeking out old public libraries. Instead, the claim is true despite the previous claim.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323042,"updateDate":1730147323042}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323042, 1730147323042),
    ($SATQ$de01ccef$SATQ$, $SATQ$7ba8f9bf-566c-4c93-88c3-ef072c125b0c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>The background colors of US and UK road signs are used to denote each sign&rsquo;s purpose.</li>
<li>Directional signs are a type of sign containing information such as route names, distance to a destination, etc.</li>
<li>Highways, major roadways, and minor roadways in the US generally use green for directional signs.</li>
<li>Highways in the UK generally use blue for directional signs.</li>
<li>Major roadways in the UK generally use green for directional signs.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to contrast how green backgrounds are used in US and UK road signs. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3ef113db-4e50-46e8-915b-fb1993468c38","content":"<p>Blue backgrounds are generally used on directional highway signs in the UK, in contrast to the green highway signs used in the US.</p>"},{"id":"3a1048d5-2d69-4455-a784-d6a16f55fbb5","content":"<p>In the US, green signs indicate directional information on both highways and major roadways, but in the UK, directional signs of this color generally appear only on major roadways.</p>"},{"id":"feea916f-aa2a-445c-8707-3a4401512f07","content":"<p>Green road signs are used in both the US and UK to denote directional information on major roadways, like distance to a destination or route names.</p>"},{"id":"a9903867-5cbd-4c23-9226-60e8e5f4630f","content":"<p>Both the UK and the US use directional signs, which include information on route names and distance to a destination.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3a1048d5-2d69-4455-a784-d6a16f55fbb5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence contrasts how green backgrounds are used in US and UK road signs, noting that the US uses them for both highways and major roadways while the UK uses them only for major roadways.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence does contrast US and UK road signs, the contrast focuses on the use of blue versus green backgrounds rather than on the use of green backgrounds specifically. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence indicates a similarity between the uses of green road signs in the US and the UK rather than contrasting them. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence indicates a similarity between road signs in the US and those in the UK; it doesn&rsquo;t contrast how green backgrounds are used in each country&rsquo;s signs.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"de01ccef","external_id":"7ba8f9bf-566c-4c93-88c3-ef072c125b0c","vaultid":null,"uId":"85bf52c8-40b3-4eb0-84be-749434bd1727","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The background colors of US and UK road signs are used to denote each sign&rsquo;s purpose.</li>\n<li>Directional signs are a type of sign containing information such as route names, distance to a destination, etc.</li>\n<li>Highways, major roadways, and minor roadways in the US generally use green for directional signs.</li>\n<li>Highways in the UK generally use blue for directional signs.</li>\n<li>Major roadways in the UK generally use green for directional signs.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to contrast how green backgrounds are used in US and UK road signs. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3ef113db-4e50-46e8-915b-fb1993468c38","content":"<p>Blue backgrounds are generally used on directional highway signs in the UK, in contrast to the green highway signs used in the US.</p>"},{"id":"3a1048d5-2d69-4455-a784-d6a16f55fbb5","content":"<p>In the US, green signs indicate directional information on both highways and major roadways, but in the UK, directional signs of this color generally appear only on major roadways.</p>"},{"id":"feea916f-aa2a-445c-8707-3a4401512f07","content":"<p>Green road signs are used in both the US and UK to denote directional information on major roadways, like distance to a destination or route names.</p>"},{"id":"a9903867-5cbd-4c23-9226-60e8e5f4630f","content":"<p>Both the UK and the US use directional signs, which include information on route names and distance to a destination.</p>"}],"keys":["3a1048d5-2d69-4455-a784-d6a16f55fbb5"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence contrasts how green backgrounds are used in US and UK road signs, noting that the US uses them for both highways and major roadways while the UK uses them only for major roadways.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence does contrast US and UK road signs, the contrast focuses on the use of blue versus green backgrounds rather than on the use of green backgrounds specifically. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence indicates a similarity between the uses of green road signs in the US and the UK rather than contrasting them. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence indicates a similarity between road signs in the US and those in the UK; it doesn&rsquo;t contrast how green backgrounds are used in each country&rsquo;s signs.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323035,"updateDate":1730147323035}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323035, 1730147323035),
    ($SATQ$de0bcf4f$SATQ$, $SATQ$9edb78a5-5dbc-486f-81dc-a9890490260d$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Spanish surrealist Oscar Dominguez, like many of his contemporaries, wanted to incorporate elements of chance and randomness in his artistic process. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> he employed techniques that produced random, unpredictable results, such as decalcomania, which involved pressing a blank canvas onto a paint-covered surface to generate abstract patterns.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"19b52753-8ecf-453c-933f-a6006287863b","content":"<p>With this in mind,</p>"},{"id":"bfe313cb-85eb-4328-9091-31cadb35abf2","content":"<p>On the contrary,</p>"},{"id":"461b0f96-2ee9-4a3a-b90e-30a6c4a3cb9c","content":"<p>In conclusion,</p>"},{"id":"241ef3ed-b802-427f-8d5d-73d0b2f9ab76","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["19b52753-8ecf-453c-933f-a6006287863b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. "With this in mind" logically signals that the activity described in this sentence&mdash;Dominguez&rsquo;s use of techniques like decalcomania to produce unpredictable abstract patterns&mdash;is a result of his desire to include random elements in his art.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. "On the contrary" illogically signals that the activity in this sentence opposes or is contrary to Dominguez&rsquo;s desire to use random elements in his art. Instead, his use of decalcomania is a result of that desire. Choice C is incorrect. "In conclusion" illogically signals that the activity in this sentence is a conclusion or summary of Dominguez&rsquo;s desire to use random elements in his art. Instead, his use of decalcomania is a result of that desire. Choice D is incorrect. "Regardless" illogically signals that the activity in this sentence occurs despite Dominguez&rsquo;s desire to use random elements in his art. Instead, his use of decalcomania is a result of that desire.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"de0bcf4f","external_id":"9edb78a5-5dbc-486f-81dc-a9890490260d","vaultid":null,"uId":"ef0ee620-a906-42c9-a9d5-e0399bfe171c","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Spanish surrealist Oscar Dominguez, like many of his contemporaries, wanted to incorporate elements of chance and randomness in his artistic process. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> he employed techniques that produced random, unpredictable results, such as decalcomania, which involved pressing a blank canvas onto a paint-covered surface to generate abstract patterns.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"19b52753-8ecf-453c-933f-a6006287863b","content":"<p>With this in mind,</p>"},{"id":"bfe313cb-85eb-4328-9091-31cadb35abf2","content":"<p>On the contrary,</p>"},{"id":"461b0f96-2ee9-4a3a-b90e-30a6c4a3cb9c","content":"<p>In conclusion,</p>"},{"id":"241ef3ed-b802-427f-8d5d-73d0b2f9ab76","content":"<p>Regardless,</p>"}],"keys":["19b52753-8ecf-453c-933f-a6006287863b"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. \"With this in mind\" logically signals that the activity described in this sentence&mdash;Dominguez&rsquo;s use of techniques like decalcomania to produce unpredictable abstract patterns&mdash;is a result of his desire to include random elements in his art.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. \"On the contrary\" illogically signals that the activity in this sentence opposes or is contrary to Dominguez&rsquo;s desire to use random elements in his art. Instead, his use of decalcomania is a result of that desire. Choice C is incorrect. \"In conclusion\" illogically signals that the activity in this sentence is a conclusion or summary of Dominguez&rsquo;s desire to use random elements in his art. Instead, his use of decalcomania is a result of that desire. Choice D is incorrect. \"Regardless\" illogically signals that the activity in this sentence occurs despite Dominguez&rsquo;s desire to use random elements in his art. Instead, his use of decalcomania is a result of that desire.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323044,"updateDate":1730147323044}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323044, 1730147323044),
    ($SATQ$dede8260$SATQ$, $SATQ$4404a2b9-0e73-42a1-9d83-4f0019e197aa$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ef345199-a37d-4d28-b5f8-472e51b199da$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>When medical students mention their patients on social media, they may violate patient confidentiality.</li>
<li>Terry Kind led a study to determine how many medical schools have student policies that mention social media use.</li>
<li>Kind and her team reviewed 132 medical school websites, examining publicly available student policies.</li>
<li>Only thirteen medical schools had guidelines that explicitly mention social media, and only five defined what constitutes acceptable social media use.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize the study&rsquo;s methodology. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"99baa3dc-a960-4f47-a05b-4122436f453e","content":"<p>The student policies of 132 medical schools can be found online, according to research by Terry Kind.</p>"},{"id":"ff3c2391-0890-4cbc-8682-0dfd84ffd612","content":"<p>To find out how many medical schools have guidelines about student social media use, Terry Kind and her team examined the student policies of 132 medical schools.</p>"},{"id":"b0c3483f-0a70-4026-bb24-737b1759442f","content":"<p>Out of 132 medical schools, only thirteen had student policies that mentioned social media, and only five specified what use was acceptable.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"34efde2a-2379-460a-a151-f65451749d80","content":"<p>Terry Kind and her team wanted to know how many medical schools have student social media policies in place about protecting patient confidentiality.&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ff3c2391-0890-4cbc-8682-0dfd84ffd612"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence effectively emphasizes Kind&rsquo;s methodology: examining the student policies of 132 medical schools for guidelines about student social media use. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence specifies how many medical schools&rsquo; student policies are available online; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the study&rsquo;s methodology. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the study&rsquo;s results, not the study&rsquo;s methodology. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the aim of the study, not the study&rsquo;s methodology. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-720-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$c6b2621d-9a9b-4f22-a5a2-26f631259228$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"dede8260","external_id":"4404a2b9-0e73-42a1-9d83-4f0019e197aa","vaultid":"ef345199-a37d-4d28-b5f8-472e51b199da","uId":"7d9dcd0d-8ca3-4731-adfc-514ccb84b37a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When medical students mention their patients on social media, they may violate patient confidentiality.</li>\n<li>Terry Kind led a study to determine how many medical schools have student policies that mention social media use.</li>\n<li>Kind and her team reviewed 132 medical school websites, examining publicly available student policies.</li>\n<li>Only thirteen medical schools had guidelines that explicitly mention social media, and only five defined what constitutes acceptable social media use.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize the study&rsquo;s methodology. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"99baa3dc-a960-4f47-a05b-4122436f453e","content":"<p>The student policies of 132 medical schools can be found online, according to research by Terry Kind.</p>"},{"id":"ff3c2391-0890-4cbc-8682-0dfd84ffd612","content":"<p>To find out how many medical schools have guidelines about student social media use, Terry Kind and her team examined the student policies of 132 medical schools.</p>"},{"id":"b0c3483f-0a70-4026-bb24-737b1759442f","content":"<p>Out of 132 medical schools, only thirteen had student policies that mentioned social media, and only five specified what use was acceptable.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"34efde2a-2379-460a-a151-f65451749d80","content":"<p>Terry Kind and her team wanted to know how many medical schools have student social media policies in place about protecting patient confidentiality.&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["ff3c2391-0890-4cbc-8682-0dfd84ffd612"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence effectively emphasizes Kind&rsquo;s methodology: examining the student policies of 132 medical schools for guidelines about student social media use. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence specifies how many medical schools&rsquo; student policies are available online; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize the study&rsquo;s methodology. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the study&rsquo;s results, not the study&rsquo;s methodology. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the aim of the study, not the study&rsquo;s methodology. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-720-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"c6b2621d-9a9b-4f22-a5a2-26f631259228","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959348,"updateDate":1691007959348}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959348, 1691007959348),
    ($SATQ$e0bd4f8a$SATQ$, $SATQ$96bc2934-6a07-464c-942c-88da8921cec0$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In 1942, the 1,500-mile Alaska Highway was constructed in under nine months, largely due to the skilled work of nearly 4,000 African American soldiers from US Army engineering regiments. The soldiers&rsquo; contribution was overlooked for decades. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> in 2017, lawmakers declared October 25 a day of recognition&mdash;&ldquo;Alaska Highway Day&rdquo;&mdash;for the troops who helped build this critical roadway.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0a8818ca-213a-45bf-870f-a885dd0b9bcc","content":"<p>Lastly,</p>"},{"id":"26636e16-9801-4a9f-a017-ffe5df006990","content":"<p>Then,</p>"},{"id":"50a7db8a-4653-49ec-ada7-12df22c771f3","content":"<p>Similarly,</p>"},{"id":"9b0ca8f6-35bb-4065-b46b-d1a0eb2a2deb","content":"<p>For example,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["26636e16-9801-4a9f-a017-ffe5df006990"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. "Then" logically signals that the event described in this sentence&mdash;lawmakers&rsquo; 2017 declaration of Alaska Highway Day&mdash;is part of a chronological sequence of events, occurring after the decades-long period in which the soldiers&rsquo; contribution was overlooked.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "lastly" illogically signals that this sentence presents the last of a series of points or reasons. Instead, it describes a later event occurring in a chronological sequence of events. Choice C is incorrect because "similarly" illogically signals that the information in this sentence is similar to the previous information about the soldiers&rsquo; contribution being overlooked for decades. Instead, it describes an event occurring after that decades-long period. Choice D is incorrect because "for example" illogically signals that this sentence provides an example illustrating the previous information about the soldiers&rsquo; contribution being overlooked for decades. Instead, it describes an event occurring after that decades-long period.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e0bd4f8a","external_id":"96bc2934-6a07-464c-942c-88da8921cec0","vaultid":null,"uId":"02b6598d-9f36-4673-bcdc-29dde6456452","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In 1942, the 1,500-mile Alaska Highway was constructed in under nine months, largely due to the skilled work of nearly 4,000 African American soldiers from US Army engineering regiments. The soldiers&rsquo; contribution was overlooked for decades. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> in 2017, lawmakers declared October 25 a day of recognition&mdash;&ldquo;Alaska Highway Day&rdquo;&mdash;for the troops who helped build this critical roadway.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0a8818ca-213a-45bf-870f-a885dd0b9bcc","content":"<p>Lastly,</p>"},{"id":"26636e16-9801-4a9f-a017-ffe5df006990","content":"<p>Then,</p>"},{"id":"50a7db8a-4653-49ec-ada7-12df22c771f3","content":"<p>Similarly,</p>"},{"id":"9b0ca8f6-35bb-4065-b46b-d1a0eb2a2deb","content":"<p>For example,</p>"}],"keys":["26636e16-9801-4a9f-a017-ffe5df006990"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. \"Then\" logically signals that the event described in this sentence&mdash;lawmakers&rsquo; 2017 declaration of Alaska Highway Day&mdash;is part of a chronological sequence of events, occurring after the decades-long period in which the soldiers&rsquo; contribution was overlooked.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"lastly\" illogically signals that this sentence presents the last of a series of points or reasons. Instead, it describes a later event occurring in a chronological sequence of events. Choice C is incorrect because \"similarly\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence is similar to the previous information about the soldiers&rsquo; contribution being overlooked for decades. Instead, it describes an event occurring after that decades-long period. Choice D is incorrect because \"for example\" illogically signals that this sentence provides an example illustrating the previous information about the soldiers&rsquo; contribution being overlooked for decades. Instead, it describes an event occurring after that decades-long period.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323044,"updateDate":1730147323044}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323044, 1730147323044),
    ($SATQ$e1453c88$SATQ$, $SATQ$0b406856-4131-43d4-a343-4d2db939e35e$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li><span data-ssml-say-as="date">1914</span>: British explorer Ernest Shackleton and a small crew embarked on an expedition to Antarctica.</li>
<li><span data-ssml-say-as="date">1915</span>: Shackleton&rsquo;s ship <em>Endurance</em> became stuck in ice before eventually breaking apart and sinking.</li>
<li><span data-ssml-say-as="date">1916</span>: After more harrowing sea-ice adventures, the entire crew was rescued.</li>
<li><span data-ssml-say-as="date">1959</span>: Historian Alfred Lansing wrote a book called <em>Endurance: Shackleton&rsquo;s Incredible Voyage</em><em>.</em>&nbsp;</li>
<li><span data-ssml-say-as="date">2001</span>: Filmmaker George Butler released a documentary called <em>The Endurance: Shackleton&rsquo;s Legendary Antarctic Expedition</em>.</li>
<li><span data-ssml-say-as="date">2022</span>: The wreckage of <em>Endurance</em> was discovered at the bottom of Antarctica&rsquo;s Weddell Sea.</li>
</ul></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to provide a historical overview of the Shackleton expedition. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"fa0ea600-af25-41f1-a469-f2de4bc75d80","content":"<p>Leaving in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1914</span> for Antarctica, Shackleton and his crew underwent many harrowing sea-ice adventures, including losing their ship in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1915</span>, before being rescued in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1916</span>.</p>"},{"id":"c5f9b548-4ccc-4f7e-bcfd-5bcaccfc5043","content":"<p>In <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1914</span>, the Shackleton expedition sailed to Antarctica, where, in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1916</span>, they rescued the crew of a ship that had sunk, <em>Endurance</em> (the wreckage of which was discovered in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2022</span>).</p>"},{"id":"59b68ed8-1b74-4535-891c-84b1ca2c2a7f","content":"<p>Shackleton&rsquo;s expedition has inspired a <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1959</span> book, a <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2001</span> film, and a <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2022</span> discovery.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"82ff706e-e41b-49a6-bab7-73a736658a7a","content":"<p>Alfred Lansing wrote about the history of Shackleton&rsquo;s 1914<span data-ssml-sub-alias=\" to \">&ndash;</span>16 expedition in the book <em>Endurance: Shackleton&rsquo;s Incredible Voyage</em> (<span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1959</span>); years later, in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2001</span>, George Butler released a documentary about the expedition.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["fa0ea600-af25-41f1-a469-f2de4bc75d80"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence provides a historical overview of the Shackleton expedition, noting that the explorers left for Antarctica in 1914, lost their ship in 1915, and were rescued in 1916.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. The sentence misrepresents information from the notes; Shackleton and his crew were themselves rescued in 1916&mdash;they weren&rsquo;t rescuing others. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence provides examples of works and discoveries inspired by the expedition; it doesn&rsquo;t provide an overview of the expedition itself. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence provides examples of works made about the expedition; it doesn&rsquo;t provide an overview of the expedition itself.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e1453c88","external_id":"0b406856-4131-43d4-a343-4d2db939e35e","vaultid":null,"uId":"fd0dd9ea-215d-4d87-a679-6a4c542832bd","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p><p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1914</span>: British explorer Ernest Shackleton and a small crew embarked on an expedition to Antarctica.</li>\n<li><span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1915</span>: Shackleton&rsquo;s ship <em>Endurance</em> became stuck in ice before eventually breaking apart and sinking.</li>\n<li><span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1916</span>: After more harrowing sea-ice adventures, the entire crew was rescued.</li>\n<li><span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1959</span>: Historian Alfred Lansing wrote a book called <em>Endurance: Shackleton&rsquo;s Incredible Voyage</em><em>.</em>&nbsp;</li>\n<li><span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2001</span>: Filmmaker George Butler released a documentary called <em>The Endurance: Shackleton&rsquo;s Legendary Antarctic Expedition</em>.</li>\n<li><span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2022</span>: The wreckage of <em>Endurance</em> was discovered at the bottom of Antarctica&rsquo;s Weddell Sea.</li>\n</ul></p>","stem":"<p>The student wants to provide a historical overview of the Shackleton expedition. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"fa0ea600-af25-41f1-a469-f2de4bc75d80","content":"<p>Leaving in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1914</span> for Antarctica, Shackleton and his crew underwent many harrowing sea-ice adventures, including losing their ship in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1915</span>, before being rescued in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1916</span>.</p>"},{"id":"c5f9b548-4ccc-4f7e-bcfd-5bcaccfc5043","content":"<p>In <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1914</span>, the Shackleton expedition sailed to Antarctica, where, in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1916</span>, they rescued the crew of a ship that had sunk, <em>Endurance</em> (the wreckage of which was discovered in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2022</span>).</p>"},{"id":"59b68ed8-1b74-4535-891c-84b1ca2c2a7f","content":"<p>Shackleton&rsquo;s expedition has inspired a <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1959</span> book, a <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2001</span> film, and a <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2022</span> discovery.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"82ff706e-e41b-49a6-bab7-73a736658a7a","content":"<p>Alfred Lansing wrote about the history of Shackleton&rsquo;s 1914<span data-ssml-sub-alias=\" to \">&ndash;</span>16 expedition in the book <em>Endurance: Shackleton&rsquo;s Incredible Voyage</em> (<span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">1959</span>); years later, in <span data-ssml-say-as=\"date\">2001</span>, George Butler released a documentary about the expedition.</p>"}],"keys":["fa0ea600-af25-41f1-a469-f2de4bc75d80"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence provides a historical overview of the Shackleton expedition, noting that the explorers left for Antarctica in 1914, lost their ship in 1915, and were rescued in 1916.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. The sentence misrepresents information from the notes; Shackleton and his crew were themselves rescued in 1916&mdash;they weren&rsquo;t rescuing others. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence provides examples of works and discoveries inspired by the expedition; it doesn&rsquo;t provide an overview of the expedition itself. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence provides examples of works made about the expedition; it doesn&rsquo;t provide an overview of the expedition itself.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771167,"updateDate":1776362771167}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771167, 1776362771167),
    ($SATQ$e1b00a70$SATQ$, $SATQ$488f2a13-c361-4378-acf9-b34bbb6267c4$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ef0948e5-0c17-47ed-b5fb-7b5439a01072$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The more diverse and wide ranging an animal&rsquo;s behaviors, the larger and more energy demanding the animal&rsquo;s brain tends to be.  <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> from an evolutionary perspective, animals that perform only basic actions should allocate fewer resources to growing and maintaining brain tissue. The specialized subtypes of ants within colonies provide an opportunity to explore this hypothesis.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"268c4179-bc36-4e68-80c5-c8ab98d3796b","content":"<p>Subsequently,</p>"},{"id":"9d002791-01b6-4eb5-9a0c-8f4bf57659ca","content":"<p>Besides,</p>"},{"id":"c1bb0d66-90d6-48c2-930e-fb93bfcea7a4","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"fef1a796-0186-4242-8abb-ddac8a808858","content":"<p>Thus,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["fef1a796-0186-4242-8abb-ddac8a808858"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;Thus&rdquo; logically signals that the claim in this sentence&mdash;that animals performing only basic actions should allocate relatively few resources to their brain tissue&mdash;is a consequence of the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains (namely, that the more diverse an animal&rsquo;s behaviors, the more energy its brain needs).&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;subsequently&rdquo; illogically signals that the claim in this sentence occurs later in a chronological sequence of events than the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains. Instead, the second claim is a consequence of the first. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;besides&rdquo; illogically signals that the claim in this sentence provides a separate point in addition to, or apart from, the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains. Instead, the second claim is a consequence of the first. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;nevertheless&rdquo; illogically signals that the claim in this sentence is true in spite of the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains. Instead, the second claim is a consequence of the first. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-215-TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$14fd89fa-20b1-4858-ad7a-d3bd8428871f$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e1b00a70","external_id":"488f2a13-c361-4378-acf9-b34bbb6267c4","vaultid":"ef0948e5-0c17-47ed-b5fb-7b5439a01072","uId":"6eb8c6e8-3536-4200-b010-e447d1e9afe3","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The more diverse and wide ranging an animal&rsquo;s behaviors, the larger and more energy demanding the animal&rsquo;s brain tends to be.  <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> from an evolutionary perspective, animals that perform only basic actions should allocate fewer resources to growing and maintaining brain tissue. The specialized subtypes of ants within colonies provide an opportunity to explore this hypothesis.&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"268c4179-bc36-4e68-80c5-c8ab98d3796b","content":"<p>Subsequently,</p>"},{"id":"9d002791-01b6-4eb5-9a0c-8f4bf57659ca","content":"<p>Besides,</p>"},{"id":"c1bb0d66-90d6-48c2-930e-fb93bfcea7a4","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"fef1a796-0186-4242-8abb-ddac8a808858","content":"<p>Thus,</p>"}],"keys":["fef1a796-0186-4242-8abb-ddac8a808858"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;Thus&rdquo; logically signals that the claim in this sentence&mdash;that animals performing only basic actions should allocate relatively few resources to their brain tissue&mdash;is a consequence of the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains (namely, that the more diverse an animal&rsquo;s behaviors, the more energy its brain needs).&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;subsequently&rdquo; illogically signals that the claim in this sentence occurs later in a chronological sequence of events than the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains. Instead, the second claim is a consequence of the first. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;besides&rdquo; illogically signals that the claim in this sentence provides a separate point in addition to, or apart from, the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains. Instead, the second claim is a consequence of the first. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;nevertheless&rdquo; illogically signals that the claim in this sentence is true in spite of the previous sentence&rsquo;s claim about the energy demands of animal brains. Instead, the second claim is a consequence of the first. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-215-TRA","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"14fd89fa-20b1-4858-ad7a-d3bd8428871f","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959327,"updateDate":1691007959327}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959327, 1691007959327),
    ($SATQ$e268c452$SATQ$, $SATQ$97d4e00a-62bc-4d6e-9499-dbdbd7288683$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The traditional process of Turkish paper marbling (<span lang="tr">ebru</span>) generally proceeds like this: First, the artisan fills a shallow tray with a water bath solution. Next, the artisan adds inks or paints to the solution, which can then be manipulated into intricate designs. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> the artisan slips paper in and out of the liquid, transferring the design onto the paper.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f03bd83c-9ac4-4e6d-8d7b-6798e2ade3f7","content":"<p>Actually,</p>"},{"id":"5580affe-7751-49f4-a2ee-a899429d91a2","content":"<p>Therefore,</p>"},{"id":"8238adbe-d512-4dd2-a79a-e402f31b0219","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"9afc44c3-e9ed-494d-8b88-d1919504664e","content":"<p>Finally,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9afc44c3-e9ed-494d-8b88-d1919504664e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;Finally&rdquo; logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that the artisan slips paper in and out of the liquid to transfer the design onto paper&mdash;is the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling, which began with what happens &ldquo;first&rdquo; (filling a tray with a solution) and continued with what happens &ldquo;next&rdquo; (adding inks or paints to the solution).</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;actually&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about slipping paper in and out of liquid to transfer a design onto paper is unexpected in light of the previously described steps. Instead, the sentence describes the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;therefore&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about slipping paper in and out of liquid to transfer a design onto paper is a consequence of the previously described steps. Instead, the sentence describes the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;nevertheless&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about slipping paper in and out of liquid to transfer a design onto paper contrasts with the previously described steps. Instead, the sentence describes the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e268c452","external_id":"97d4e00a-62bc-4d6e-9499-dbdbd7288683","vaultid":null,"uId":"aa484fe7-aeca-44d0-a576-eba325ff837f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The traditional process of Turkish paper marbling (<span lang=\"tr\">ebru</span>) generally proceeds like this: First, the artisan fills a shallow tray with a water bath solution. Next, the artisan adds inks or paints to the solution, which can then be manipulated into intricate designs. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> the artisan slips paper in and out of the liquid, transferring the design onto the paper.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f03bd83c-9ac4-4e6d-8d7b-6798e2ade3f7","content":"<p>Actually,</p>"},{"id":"5580affe-7751-49f4-a2ee-a899429d91a2","content":"<p>Therefore,</p>"},{"id":"8238adbe-d512-4dd2-a79a-e402f31b0219","content":"<p>Nevertheless,</p>"},{"id":"9afc44c3-e9ed-494d-8b88-d1919504664e","content":"<p>Finally,</p>"}],"keys":["9afc44c3-e9ed-494d-8b88-d1919504664e"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;Finally&rdquo; logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that the artisan slips paper in and out of the liquid to transfer the design onto paper&mdash;is the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling, which began with what happens &ldquo;first&rdquo; (filling a tray with a solution) and continued with what happens &ldquo;next&rdquo; (adding inks or paints to the solution).</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;actually&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about slipping paper in and out of liquid to transfer a design onto paper is unexpected in light of the previously described steps. Instead, the sentence describes the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;therefore&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about slipping paper in and out of liquid to transfer a design onto paper is a consequence of the previously described steps. Instead, the sentence describes the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;nevertheless&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about slipping paper in and out of liquid to transfer a design onto paper contrasts with the previously described steps. Instead, the sentence describes the final step in the process of Turkish paper marbling.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771169,"updateDate":1776362771169}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771169, 1776362771169),
    ($SATQ$e2693197$SATQ$, $SATQ$ecd2318b-8cde-4df7-aedd-6cfb3adcb71a$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$39f34650-414d-4f08-8efc-ef0bbd977b6e$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li><em>Oracles of the Pink Universe</em> was a 2021 exhibition at the Denver Museum of Art in Colorado.</li>
<li>It featured eight artworks by South African artist Simphiwe Ndzube.</li>
<li>One of these works is a painting titled <em>Assertion of Will</em>.</li>
<li><em>Assertion of Will</em> depicts three standing figures.</li>
<li>The figures wear clothing made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting&rsquo;s canvas.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to describe how fabric is used in <em>Assertion of Will</em>. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0176bccb-0203-4289-8b8e-0b06774bd458","content":"<p>In <em>Assertion of Will</em>, the figures&rsquo; clothing is made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting&rsquo;s canvas.</p>"},{"id":"899d8e6c-d1e2-4cee-81e9-8058ef8bc22d","content":"<p>The exhibition <em>Oracles of the Pink Universe</em> featured artworks by artist Simphiwe Ndzube.</p>"},{"id":"44a8e16a-39b4-401e-9cdf-40b8bfbfa8d1","content":"<p>Depicting three standing, clothed figures, <em>Assertion of Will</em> is a painting by Simphiwe Ndzube.</p>"},{"id":"d79e046c-7953-4b77-94b5-298b9dd84b48","content":"<p>Simphiwe Ndzube&rsquo;s <em>Assertion of Will</em> was one of eight artworks exhibited in <em>Oracles of the Pink Universe</em> at the Denver Museum of Art.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0176bccb-0203-4289-8b8e-0b06774bd458"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. This choice directly describes how fabric is used in <em>Assertion of Will</em>, by explaining that the fabric pieces are part of the painting itself.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice provides contextual information about the exhibition, but it doesn&rsquo;t mention anything about the painting or the fabric.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. This choice mentions that the figures are clothed, but it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the fabric is integrated into the painting.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect. This choice provides contextual information about the painting, but it doesn&rsquo;t mention anything about the fabric or how it is used.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-E006$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$652a5d2b-6057-45a6-b0e2-86cfecd4b91e$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e2693197","external_id":"ecd2318b-8cde-4df7-aedd-6cfb3adcb71a","vaultid":"39f34650-414d-4f08-8efc-ef0bbd977b6e","uId":"0ee0e83f-f428-4970-9d93-f85e34802f96","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Oracles of the Pink Universe</em> was a 2021 exhibition at the Denver Museum of Art in Colorado.</li>\n<li>It featured eight artworks by South African artist Simphiwe Ndzube.</li>\n<li>One of these works is a painting titled <em>Assertion of Will</em>.</li>\n<li><em>Assertion of Will</em> depicts three standing figures.</li>\n<li>The figures wear clothing made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting&rsquo;s canvas.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to describe how fabric is used in <em>Assertion of Will</em>. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0176bccb-0203-4289-8b8e-0b06774bd458","content":"<p>In <em>Assertion of Will</em>, the figures&rsquo; clothing is made of fabric pieces stitched to the painting&rsquo;s canvas.</p>"},{"id":"899d8e6c-d1e2-4cee-81e9-8058ef8bc22d","content":"<p>The exhibition <em>Oracles of the Pink Universe</em> featured artworks by artist Simphiwe Ndzube.</p>"},{"id":"44a8e16a-39b4-401e-9cdf-40b8bfbfa8d1","content":"<p>Depicting three standing, clothed figures, <em>Assertion of Will</em> is a painting by Simphiwe Ndzube.</p>"},{"id":"d79e046c-7953-4b77-94b5-298b9dd84b48","content":"<p>Simphiwe Ndzube&rsquo;s <em>Assertion of Will</em> was one of eight artworks exhibited in <em>Oracles of the Pink Universe</em> at the Denver Museum of Art.</p>"}],"keys":["0176bccb-0203-4289-8b8e-0b06774bd458"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. This choice directly describes how fabric is used in <em>Assertion of Will</em>, by explaining that the fabric pieces are part of the painting itself.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. This choice provides contextual information about the exhibition, but it doesn&rsquo;t mention anything about the painting or the fabric.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. This choice mentions that the figures are clothed, but it doesn&rsquo;t explain how the fabric is integrated into the painting.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect. This choice provides contextual information about the painting, but it doesn&rsquo;t mention anything about the fabric or how it is used.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-E006","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"652a5d2b-6057-45a6-b0e2-86cfecd4b91e","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959371,"updateDate":1691007959371}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959371, 1691007959371),
    ($SATQ$e2d97f10$SATQ$, $SATQ$6f77f810-8fba-4625-b6e7-411afe24b747$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$a0994e32-b40f-46c6-b607-c68588b0d125$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Pterosaurs were flying reptiles that existed millions of years ago.</li>
<li>In a 2021 study, Anusuya Chinsamy-Turan analyzed fragments of pterosaur jawbones located in the Sahara Desert.</li>
<li>She was initially unsure if the bones belonged to juvenile or adult pterosaurs. </li>
<li>She used advanced microscope techniques to determine that the bones had few growth lines relative to the bones of fully grown pterosaurs.</li>
<li>She concluded that the bones belonged to juveniles.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to present the study and its findings. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e6289f76-f73c-4e9f-9443-246d21b780c6","content":"<p>In 2021, Chinsamy-Turan studied pterosaur jawbones and was initially unsure if the bones belonged to juveniles or adults.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"c3d56eab-0bf7-44bb-b321-0c6e2b5ac875","content":"<p>Pterosaur jawbones located in the Sahara Desert were the focus of a 2021 study.</p>"},{"id":"5c6f57cb-d02c-4c3d-91bb-66d7efb54902","content":"<p>In a 2021 study, Chinsamy-Turan used advanced microscope techniques to analyze the jawbones of pterosaurs, flying reptiles that existed millions of years ago.</p>"},{"id":"5f922fa9-64a9-4c05-a93b-701375c2a164","content":"<p>In a 2021 study, Chinsamy-Turan determined that pterosaur jawbones located in the Sahara Desert had few growth lines relative to the bones of fully grown pterosaurs and thus belonged to juveniles.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5f922fa9-64a9-4c05-a93b-701375c2a164"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence presents both the study and its findings, noting the study&rsquo;s date and the researcher&rsquo;s name as well as describing what the researcher determined about the jawbones and how she determined it. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence describes the study and the researcher&rsquo;s initial assessment, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s findings. Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence describes the study and its focus, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s findings or the name of the researcher who conducted it. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence mentions the study&rsquo;s methodology and provides information about pterosaurs, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s findings. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-762-SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$716e4019-1b17-4a1b-b56d-5cc6a9feb502$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e2d97f10","external_id":"6f77f810-8fba-4625-b6e7-411afe24b747","vaultid":"a0994e32-b40f-46c6-b607-c68588b0d125","uId":"6dc1b4b6-0f74-4d4c-8cdf-9efed419dee8","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pterosaurs were flying reptiles that existed millions of years ago.</li>\n<li>In a 2021 study, Anusuya Chinsamy-Turan analyzed fragments of pterosaur jawbones located in the Sahara Desert.</li>\n<li>She was initially unsure if the bones belonged to juvenile or adult pterosaurs. </li>\n<li>She used advanced microscope techniques to determine that the bones had few growth lines relative to the bones of fully grown pterosaurs.</li>\n<li>She concluded that the bones belonged to juveniles.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to present the study and its findings. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e6289f76-f73c-4e9f-9443-246d21b780c6","content":"<p>In 2021, Chinsamy-Turan studied pterosaur jawbones and was initially unsure if the bones belonged to juveniles or adults.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"c3d56eab-0bf7-44bb-b321-0c6e2b5ac875","content":"<p>Pterosaur jawbones located in the Sahara Desert were the focus of a 2021 study.</p>"},{"id":"5c6f57cb-d02c-4c3d-91bb-66d7efb54902","content":"<p>In a 2021 study, Chinsamy-Turan used advanced microscope techniques to analyze the jawbones of pterosaurs, flying reptiles that existed millions of years ago.</p>"},{"id":"5f922fa9-64a9-4c05-a93b-701375c2a164","content":"<p>In a 2021 study, Chinsamy-Turan determined that pterosaur jawbones located in the Sahara Desert had few growth lines relative to the bones of fully grown pterosaurs and thus belonged to juveniles.</p>"}],"keys":["5f922fa9-64a9-4c05-a93b-701375c2a164"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence presents both the study and its findings, noting the study&rsquo;s date and the researcher&rsquo;s name as well as describing what the researcher determined about the jawbones and how she determined it. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence describes the study and the researcher&rsquo;s initial assessment, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s findings. Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence describes the study and its focus, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s findings or the name of the researcher who conducted it. Choice C is incorrect. While the sentence mentions the study&rsquo;s methodology and provides information about pterosaurs, it doesn&rsquo;t present the study&rsquo;s findings. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-762-SYN","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"716e4019-1b17-4a1b-b56d-5cc6a9feb502","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959351,"updateDate":1691007959351}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959351, 1691007959351),
    ($SATQ$e2eb70b9$SATQ$, $SATQ$fc018601-4465-4f04-82ee-06f6db2cf75b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Traditionally, manufacturers have dyed denim jeans blue by dipping them in a solution containing indigo powder.</li>
<li>Indigo doesn&rsquo;t dissolve in just water, so manufacturers must mix hazardous chemicals with water to dissolve the powder.</li>
<li>Textile researcher Smriti Rai discovered a process for dyeing blue jeans without chemicals.</li>
<li>Rai added indigo powder to a hydrogel containing nanocellulose and produced a dye that could be spread directly onto the denim.</li>
<li>Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3456de17-f0ee-41eb-8b58-133f415d7f74","content":"<p>Though created using a different process, Rai&rsquo;s dye contains the same ingredient as the dye produced by blue jean manufacturers.</p>"},{"id":"ef55ea77-e828-4486-aabe-d8235a402217","content":"<p>Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder, which doesn&rsquo;t dissolve in water.</p>"},{"id":"7c9118d8-6ed3-4029-b265-9bbaaaa2fb60","content":"<p>The traditional approach to dyeing blue jeans is to dip them in a solution containing hazardous chemicals.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"80fb7e8b-36c7-4031-90b3-da0425f18109","content":"<p>Rai&rsquo;s approach substitutes a natural, plant-based substance for the hazardous chemicals that manufacturers have traditionally used.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["80fb7e8b-36c7-4031-90b3-da0425f18109"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans, noting that Rai&rsquo;s approach uses a natural, plant-based substance in place of hazardous chemicals.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between the dyes used in the two approaches, noting that the dyes contain the same ingredient; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence explains what nanocellulose is; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence explains the traditional approach to dyeing blue jeans; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the traditional approach and Rai&rsquo;s approach.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e2eb70b9","external_id":"fc018601-4465-4f04-82ee-06f6db2cf75b","vaultid":null,"uId":"d6290dc3-34f2-40d8-b903-71c2e57854f9","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Traditionally, manufacturers have dyed denim jeans blue by dipping them in a solution containing indigo powder.</li>\n<li>Indigo doesn&rsquo;t dissolve in just water, so manufacturers must mix hazardous chemicals with water to dissolve the powder.</li>\n<li>Textile researcher Smriti Rai discovered a process for dyeing blue jeans without chemicals.</li>\n<li>Rai added indigo powder to a hydrogel containing nanocellulose and produced a dye that could be spread directly onto the denim.</li>\n<li>Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3456de17-f0ee-41eb-8b58-133f415d7f74","content":"<p>Though created using a different process, Rai&rsquo;s dye contains the same ingredient as the dye produced by blue jean manufacturers.</p>"},{"id":"ef55ea77-e828-4486-aabe-d8235a402217","content":"<p>Nanocellulose is a natural, plant-based substance that separates the molecules of indigo powder, which doesn&rsquo;t dissolve in water.</p>"},{"id":"7c9118d8-6ed3-4029-b265-9bbaaaa2fb60","content":"<p>The traditional approach to dyeing blue jeans is to dip them in a solution containing hazardous chemicals.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"80fb7e8b-36c7-4031-90b3-da0425f18109","content":"<p>Rai&rsquo;s approach substitutes a natural, plant-based substance for the hazardous chemicals that manufacturers have traditionally used.</p>"}],"keys":["80fb7e8b-36c7-4031-90b3-da0425f18109"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans, noting that Rai&rsquo;s approach uses a natural, plant-based substance in place of hazardous chemicals.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between the dyes used in the two approaches, noting that the dyes contain the same ingredient; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence explains what nanocellulose is; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the two approaches to dyeing blue jeans. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence explains the traditional approach to dyeing blue jeans; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the traditional approach and Rai&rsquo;s approach.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323048,"updateDate":1730147323048}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323048, 1730147323048),
    ($SATQ$e3484c07$SATQ$, $SATQ$5a0e2241-ed38-4728-b7c3-3ed01e67e6cb$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$760e40e6-07a1-4e72-af45-465c4d3d431f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bioluminescence is the emission of light by living organisms.</li>
<li>This light is produced by chemical reactions in organisms&rsquo; cells.</li>
<li>Jellyfish emit flashes of blue light.</li>
<li>This behavior serves to startle predators.</li>
<li>Black dragonfish emit a steady red light.</li>
<li>This behavior helps them locate prey in deep waters.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a difference between the behavior of jellyfish and that of black dragonfish. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2457aba7-1609-4788-adc2-4ca8994e12fa","content":"<p>Both jellyfish and black dragonfish are organisms that emit light, which is produced by chemical reactions in these organisms&rsquo; cells.</p>"},{"id":"6eac3b97-15b6-4c47-bb6e-1e893baa69bb","content":"<p>Black dragonfish emit a steady red light, which helps them locate prey in deep waters.</p>"},{"id":"433ecdb6-fdcd-4ff2-b057-73465c658d66","content":"<p>Bioluminescence, the emission of light by living organisms, results from chemical reactions in organisms&rsquo; cells.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"ba72c8cc-b3d5-49a5-b4fb-9acf405e12fb","content":"<p>Jellyfish emit light to startle predators, whereas black dragonfish do so to locate prey.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ba72c8cc-b3d5-49a5-b4fb-9acf405e12fb"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a difference between the behavior of jellyfish and that of black dragonfish, noting that jellyfish and black dragonfish emit light as part of different behaviors (protection and predation, respectively). </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between jellyfish and black dragonfish; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the behavior of the two animals. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the type of bioluminescence exhibited by black dragonfish, noting that it&rsquo;s used in predation; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the behavior of the two animals. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence defines bioluminescence and explains how it works; the sentence doesn&rsquo;t mention either animal or emphasize a difference between them. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-SYN-E010$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$bb1b0949-50e9-4e2f-a6fd-440265af97ea$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e3484c07","external_id":"5a0e2241-ed38-4728-b7c3-3ed01e67e6cb","vaultid":"760e40e6-07a1-4e72-af45-465c4d3d431f","uId":"df9725e1-f5be-46b2-b003-bad2d0e161f0","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bioluminescence is the emission of light by living organisms.</li>\n<li>This light is produced by chemical reactions in organisms&rsquo; cells.</li>\n<li>Jellyfish emit flashes of blue light.</li>\n<li>This behavior serves to startle predators.</li>\n<li>Black dragonfish emit a steady red light.</li>\n<li>This behavior helps them locate prey in deep waters.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a difference between the behavior of jellyfish and that of black dragonfish. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2457aba7-1609-4788-adc2-4ca8994e12fa","content":"<p>Both jellyfish and black dragonfish are organisms that emit light, which is produced by chemical reactions in these organisms&rsquo; cells.</p>"},{"id":"6eac3b97-15b6-4c47-bb6e-1e893baa69bb","content":"<p>Black dragonfish emit a steady red light, which helps them locate prey in deep waters.</p>"},{"id":"433ecdb6-fdcd-4ff2-b057-73465c658d66","content":"<p>Bioluminescence, the emission of light by living organisms, results from chemical reactions in organisms&rsquo; cells.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"ba72c8cc-b3d5-49a5-b4fb-9acf405e12fb","content":"<p>Jellyfish emit light to startle predators, whereas black dragonfish do so to locate prey.</p>"}],"keys":["ba72c8cc-b3d5-49a5-b4fb-9acf405e12fb"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a difference between the behavior of jellyfish and that of black dragonfish, noting that jellyfish and black dragonfish emit light as part of different behaviors (protection and predation, respectively). </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between jellyfish and black dragonfish; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the behavior of the two animals. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes the type of bioluminescence exhibited by black dragonfish, noting that it&rsquo;s used in predation; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a difference between the behavior of the two animals. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence defines bioluminescence and explains how it works; the sentence doesn&rsquo;t mention either animal or emphasize a difference between them. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-SYN-E010","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"bb1b0949-50e9-4e2f-a6fd-440265af97ea","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959371,"updateDate":1691007959371}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959371, 1691007959371),
    ($SATQ$e3bbf2bf$SATQ$, $SATQ$feb2e7d3-521f-476d-97f0-b3f4e67ec2e6$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>In World War I, US soldiers who were members of the Choctaw Nation in Oklahoma participated in the Choctaw Code Talkers program.</li>
<li>The Choctaw Code Talkers were trained to relay coded military information in their native language.</li>
<li>In World War II, the US Army recruited Navajo (<span lang="nv">Din&eacute;</span>) soldiers to transmit coded messages in their native language.</li>
<li>These soldiers were known as the Navajo Code Talkers.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"6db1f467-ee53-4cd2-b89d-46364a3c910e","content":"<p>US soldiers who were members of the Choctaw Nation in Oklahoma used their native language to relay coded information.</p>"},{"id":"f3a5cb9c-2451-43d9-bb78-d170e4f34ada","content":"<p>In World War II, one group of Navajo (<span lang=\"nv\">Din&eacute;</span>) soldiers was known as the Navajo Code Talkers.</p>"},{"id":"5242ef07-ac92-40eb-8fd0-9fe3ea1148b3","content":"<p>Both the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers transmitted coded military messages in the soldiers&rsquo; native languages.</p>\n<ul/>"},{"id":"d3a89da6-6614-47c6-9956-10f0e76aa5df","content":"<p>The Choctaw Code Talkers, not the Navajo Code Talkers, served in World War I.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5242ef07-ac92-40eb-8fd0-9fe3ea1148b3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers by explaining that both groups used their native languages to transmit coded messages for the military.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence describes the Choctaw Code Talkers; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence introduces the Navajo Code Talkers; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a difference between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e3bbf2bf","external_id":"feb2e7d3-521f-476d-97f0-b3f4e67ec2e6","vaultid":null,"uId":"0bd7351e-2886-46e2-b535-64cc4368444a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In World War I, US soldiers who were members of the Choctaw Nation in Oklahoma participated in the Choctaw Code Talkers program.</li>\n<li>The Choctaw Code Talkers were trained to relay coded military information in their native language.</li>\n<li>In World War II, the US Army recruited Navajo (<span lang=\"nv\">Din&eacute;</span>) soldiers to transmit coded messages in their native language.</li>\n<li>These soldiers were known as the Navajo Code Talkers.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"6db1f467-ee53-4cd2-b89d-46364a3c910e","content":"<p>US soldiers who were members of the Choctaw Nation in Oklahoma used their native language to relay coded information.</p>"},{"id":"f3a5cb9c-2451-43d9-bb78-d170e4f34ada","content":"<p>In World War II, one group of Navajo (<span lang=\"nv\">Din&eacute;</span>) soldiers was known as the Navajo Code Talkers.</p>"},{"id":"5242ef07-ac92-40eb-8fd0-9fe3ea1148b3","content":"<p>Both the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers transmitted coded military messages in the soldiers&rsquo; native languages.</p>\n<ul/>"},{"id":"d3a89da6-6614-47c6-9956-10f0e76aa5df","content":"<p>The Choctaw Code Talkers, not the Navajo Code Talkers, served in World War I.</p>"}],"keys":["5242ef07-ac92-40eb-8fd0-9fe3ea1148b3"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers by explaining that both groups used their native languages to transmit coded messages for the military.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence describes the Choctaw Code Talkers; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence introduces the Navajo Code Talkers; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a difference between the Choctaw Code Talkers and the Navajo Code Talkers; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323032,"updateDate":1730147323032}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323032, 1730147323032),
    ($SATQ$e3edc138$SATQ$, $SATQ$c956956e-cfea-4723-b4c0-78b3b2301076$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$f428b9b7-fd04-46be-8d8b-7f2a38ded204$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In a heated debate in biogeography, the field is divided between dispersalists and vicariancists. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> there are those who argue that dispersal is the most crucial determining factor in a species&rsquo; distribution, and those who insist that vicariance (separation due to geographic barriers) is. Biogeographer Isabel Sanmart&iacute;n counts herself among neither.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"82d1c2e1-791e-469d-995f-20307492163b","content":"<p>Furthermore,</p>"},{"id":"49cff7e7-68d3-45aa-86ff-76f1540bad9f","content":"<p>By contrast,</p>"},{"id":"b66784d1-e810-4be4-97a3-5f12cfe270f0","content":"<p>Similarly,</p>"},{"id":"844e461d-3c08-4ba1-b382-d4b6f87a3200","content":"<p>That is,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["844e461d-3c08-4ba1-b382-d4b6f87a3200"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;That is&rdquo; logically signals that this sentence clarifies the terms of the scientific debate introduced in the previous sentence by explaining the difference between dispersalists and vicariancists. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;furthermore&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is merely additional to (and separate from) the information in the previous sentence about the scientific debate. Instead, the information about dispersalists and vicariancists clarifies the terms of that debate. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;by contrast&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the information in the previous sentence about the scientific debate. Instead, the information about dispersalists and vicariancists clarifies the terms of that debate. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;similarly&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is merely similar to the information in the previous sentence about the scientific debate. Instead, the information about dispersalists and vicariancists clarifies the terms of that debate. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-TRA-H001$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$80dba2b4-ec67-4663-9800-cf7bfbef6268$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e3edc138","external_id":"c956956e-cfea-4723-b4c0-78b3b2301076","vaultid":"f428b9b7-fd04-46be-8d8b-7f2a38ded204","uId":"0b1e1ae3-af3f-4364-8fde-cb096c5f206a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In a heated debate in biogeography, the field is divided between dispersalists and vicariancists. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> there are those who argue that dispersal is the most crucial determining factor in a species&rsquo; distribution, and those who insist that vicariance (separation due to geographic barriers) is. Biogeographer Isabel Sanmart&iacute;n counts herself among neither.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"82d1c2e1-791e-469d-995f-20307492163b","content":"<p>Furthermore,</p>"},{"id":"49cff7e7-68d3-45aa-86ff-76f1540bad9f","content":"<p>By contrast,</p>"},{"id":"b66784d1-e810-4be4-97a3-5f12cfe270f0","content":"<p>Similarly,</p>"},{"id":"844e461d-3c08-4ba1-b382-d4b6f87a3200","content":"<p>That is,</p>"}],"keys":["844e461d-3c08-4ba1-b382-d4b6f87a3200"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. &ldquo;That is&rdquo; logically signals that this sentence clarifies the terms of the scientific debate introduced in the previous sentence by explaining the difference between dispersalists and vicariancists. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;furthermore&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is merely additional to (and separate from) the information in the previous sentence about the scientific debate. Instead, the information about dispersalists and vicariancists clarifies the terms of that debate. Choice B is incorrect because &ldquo;by contrast&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the information in the previous sentence about the scientific debate. Instead, the information about dispersalists and vicariancists clarifies the terms of that debate. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;similarly&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence is merely similar to the information in the previous sentence about the scientific debate. Instead, the information about dispersalists and vicariancists clarifies the terms of that debate. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-TRA-H001","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"80dba2b4-ec67-4663-9800-cf7bfbef6268","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959373,"updateDate":1691007959373}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959373, 1691007959373),
    ($SATQ$e6b1e12c$SATQ$, $SATQ$02e8a6bd-5ee6-4963-a33f-b583deda3645$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Long thought to be sessile (immobile), adult <em>Chelonibia testudinaria</em>, barnacles that adhere to sea turtle shells, have been observed to shift slightly in position over time&mdash;a phenomenon that has been attributed to the barnacles&rsquo; passive displacement by water currents. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> a research team found that adult <em><span data-ssml-sub-alias="C">C.</span> testudinaria</em> moved toward the heads of their sea turtle hosts and thus against the prevailing water flow, behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0418770a-ae43-403c-abec-997accd36c26","content":"<p>Contrary to this phenomenon,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"3fabf3d9-db58-496d-9228-ead3b01bcc02","content":"<p>Undermining this explanation,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"842a6c3b-ae1c-45d2-8d01-34d3f2afb281","content":"<p>Drawing a similar conclusion,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"6e6516ad-7058-4f2b-8e72-7deaa5590f15","content":"<p>Confirming this hypothesis,</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3fabf3d9-db58-496d-9228-ead3b01bcc02"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. &ldquo;Undermining this explanation&rdquo; logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that adult <em>Chelonibia testudinaria</em> showed behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion&mdash;undermines or weakens the previous explanation that barnacle movement was a result of passive displacement by water currents.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;contrary to this phenomenon&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about barnacles exhibiting behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion opposes the previous information about barnacles shifting slightly in position over time. Instead, the sentence undermines or weakens the previous claim about passive displacement. That is, the sentence doesn&rsquo;t oppose the fact that the barnacles shifted position: it challenges the previous sentence&rsquo;s explanation for the movement. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;drawing a similar conclusion&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about barnacles exhibiting behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion is similar to the previous conclusion that barnacle movement is the result of passive displacement. Instead, the sentence undermines or weakens the previous sentence&rsquo;s explanation for how the barnacles moved. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;confirming this hypothesis&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about barnacles exhibiting behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion confirms the hypothesis in the previous sentence that the barnacle movement was the result of passive displacement. Instead, the sentence undermines or weakens the previous sentence&rsquo;s explanation for how the barnacles moved.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e6b1e12c","external_id":"02e8a6bd-5ee6-4963-a33f-b583deda3645","vaultid":null,"uId":"19906689-14f4-460e-aee8-16b913c73711","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Long thought to be sessile (immobile), adult <em>Chelonibia testudinaria</em>, barnacles that adhere to sea turtle shells, have been observed to shift slightly in position over time&mdash;a phenomenon that has been attributed to the barnacles&rsquo; passive displacement by water currents. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> a research team found that adult <em><span data-ssml-sub-alias=\"C\">C.</span> testudinaria</em> moved toward the heads of their sea turtle hosts and thus against the prevailing water flow, behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion.&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0418770a-ae43-403c-abec-997accd36c26","content":"<p>Contrary to this phenomenon,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"3fabf3d9-db58-496d-9228-ead3b01bcc02","content":"<p>Undermining this explanation,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"842a6c3b-ae1c-45d2-8d01-34d3f2afb281","content":"<p>Drawing a similar conclusion,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"6e6516ad-7058-4f2b-8e72-7deaa5590f15","content":"<p>Confirming this hypothesis,</p>"}],"keys":["3fabf3d9-db58-496d-9228-ead3b01bcc02"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. &ldquo;Undermining this explanation&rdquo; logically signals that the information in this sentence&mdash;that adult <em>Chelonibia testudinaria</em> showed behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion&mdash;undermines or weakens the previous explanation that barnacle movement was a result of passive displacement by water currents.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;contrary to this phenomenon&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about barnacles exhibiting behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion opposes the previous information about barnacles shifting slightly in position over time. Instead, the sentence undermines or weakens the previous claim about passive displacement. That is, the sentence doesn&rsquo;t oppose the fact that the barnacles shifted position: it challenges the previous sentence&rsquo;s explanation for the movement. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;drawing a similar conclusion&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about barnacles exhibiting behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion is similar to the previous conclusion that barnacle movement is the result of passive displacement. Instead, the sentence undermines or weakens the previous sentence&rsquo;s explanation for how the barnacles moved. Choice D is incorrect because &ldquo;confirming this hypothesis&rdquo; illogically signals that the information in this sentence about barnacles exhibiting behavior consistent with self-initiated locomotion confirms the hypothesis in the previous sentence that the barnacle movement was the result of passive displacement. Instead, the sentence undermines or weakens the previous sentence&rsquo;s explanation for how the barnacles moved.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771167,"updateDate":1776362771167}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771167, 1776362771167),
    ($SATQ$e6b57c9b$SATQ$, $SATQ$5a4e75f4-a147-4de8-a439-6025b2d19bb0$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Iranian scholar Abu Rayhan al-Biruni studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features.</li>
<li>He theorized that a large landmass existed west of Europe and east of Asia.</li>
<li>Al-Biruni published his landmass theory in 1037 CE.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to specify when al-Biruni published his landmass theory. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e55d6c43-45cd-4dbc-b36c-803e6f23267e","content":"<p>In 1037 CE, al-Biruni published his theory that a large landmass existed west of Europe and east of Asia.</p>"},{"id":"b0c4d050-39fa-4254-9a3a-2a5ba03a9cdb","content":"<p>Al-Biruni, who studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features, published a theory about a large landmass.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"8f64045e-4e2b-4716-961a-6021eac32834","content":"<p>Al-Biruni was an Iranian scholar who studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features.</p>"},{"id":"03a004fa-44df-485d-a35d-60f8d30f922b","content":"<p>An Iranian scholar who studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features, al-Biruni theorized that a large landmass existed west of Europe and east of Asia.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e55d6c43-45cd-4dbc-b36c-803e6f23267e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence specifies when al-Biruni published his landmass theory, indicating that it was published in the year 1037 CE.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence notes that al-Biruni published a landmass theory, it doesn&rsquo;t specify when the theory was published. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence identifies al-Biruni as a scholar of Earth&rsquo;s physical features; it doesn&rsquo;t specify when he published his landmass theory. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence describes al-Biruni&rsquo;s landmass theory; it doesn&rsquo;t specify when the theory was published.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e6b57c9b","external_id":"5a4e75f4-a147-4de8-a439-6025b2d19bb0","vaultid":null,"uId":"e597ff6b-fb50-442d-9bb0-4d395dfb9090","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Iranian scholar Abu Rayhan al-Biruni studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features.</li>\n<li>He theorized that a large landmass existed west of Europe and east of Asia.</li>\n<li>Al-Biruni published his landmass theory in 1037 CE.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to specify when al-Biruni published his landmass theory. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e55d6c43-45cd-4dbc-b36c-803e6f23267e","content":"<p>In 1037 CE, al-Biruni published his theory that a large landmass existed west of Europe and east of Asia.</p>"},{"id":"b0c4d050-39fa-4254-9a3a-2a5ba03a9cdb","content":"<p>Al-Biruni, who studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features, published a theory about a large landmass.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"8f64045e-4e2b-4716-961a-6021eac32834","content":"<p>Al-Biruni was an Iranian scholar who studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features.</p>"},{"id":"03a004fa-44df-485d-a35d-60f8d30f922b","content":"<p>An Iranian scholar who studied Earth&rsquo;s physical features, al-Biruni theorized that a large landmass existed west of Europe and east of Asia.</p>"}],"keys":["e55d6c43-45cd-4dbc-b36c-803e6f23267e"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. The sentence specifies when al-Biruni published his landmass theory, indicating that it was published in the year 1037 CE.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence notes that al-Biruni published a landmass theory, it doesn&rsquo;t specify when the theory was published. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence identifies al-Biruni as a scholar of Earth&rsquo;s physical features; it doesn&rsquo;t specify when he published his landmass theory. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence describes al-Biruni&rsquo;s landmass theory; it doesn&rsquo;t specify when the theory was published.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323033,"updateDate":1730147323033}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323033, 1730147323033),
    ($SATQ$e8494245$SATQ$, $SATQ$944d6e30-8dda-4769-bf70-e1b924a62c8c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Political scientist Graham Allison is known for his Thucydides trap theory.</li>
<li>Allison&rsquo;s theory states that whenever &ldquo;a rising power is threatening to displace a ruling power,&rdquo; conflict is likely.</li>
<li>The theory is based on Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict between Athens and Sparta.</li>
<li>Thucydides wrote that &ldquo;the rise of Athens and the fear this instilled in Sparta&rdquo; made conflict &ldquo;inevitable.&rdquo;</li>
<li>History professor Edmund Stewart recently challenged the historical basis of the theory.</li>
<li>Stewart claimed that Athens was not a rising power and that the rivals experienced a &ldquo;clash of cultures&rdquo; instead.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to use a quotation to challenge Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict between Athens and Sparta. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c1154794-1106-44bb-871d-6565cb698afc","content":"<p>According to Allison&rsquo;s Thucydides trap theory, whenever &ldquo;a rising power is threatening to displace a ruling power,&rdquo; conflict is likely.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"7c92f05f-ab22-4e85-a613-65952d081391","content":"<p>Thucydides wrote that conflict between the two powers was &ldquo;inevitable,&rdquo; although Stewart later challenged the historical basis of this claim.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"3e3c4f27-c1a4-4a79-ac5a-876af6d55a6c","content":"<p>According to Stewart, a &ldquo;clash of cultures&rdquo; between Athens and Sparta caused the conflict, not Athens&rsquo;s rise.</p>"},{"id":"e1dcce25-1dd1-4a42-9e79-87c5797827da","content":"<p>Thucydides explained that conflict was caused by &ldquo;the rise of Athens and the fear this instilled in Sparta,&rdquo; but Allison disagreed, seeing the conflict as an example of the Thucydides trap.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3e3c4f27-c1a4-4a79-ac5a-876af6d55a6c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. Using a quotation from Stewart, the sentence challenges Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation that the rise of Athens caused the conflict, suggesting that it was instead caused by a "clash of cultures."</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence uses a quotation, the quotation doesn&rsquo;t challenge Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict. Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence mentions that Stewart challenged Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict, it doesn&rsquo;t use a quotation to challenge Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation: the quoted word "inevitable" is from Thucydides. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence appears to refute Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation, it does so in a way that misrepresents the information in the notes; Allison&rsquo;s Thucydides trap theory is based on Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict. Thus, Allison&rsquo;s theory affirms, rather than challenges, Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e8494245","external_id":"944d6e30-8dda-4769-bf70-e1b924a62c8c","vaultid":null,"uId":"f550cb12-a237-4548-a71e-fe24e39ab3ac","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Political scientist Graham Allison is known for his Thucydides trap theory.</li>\n<li>Allison&rsquo;s theory states that whenever &ldquo;a rising power is threatening to displace a ruling power,&rdquo; conflict is likely.</li>\n<li>The theory is based on Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict between Athens and Sparta.</li>\n<li>Thucydides wrote that &ldquo;the rise of Athens and the fear this instilled in Sparta&rdquo; made conflict &ldquo;inevitable.&rdquo;</li>\n<li>History professor Edmund Stewart recently challenged the historical basis of the theory.</li>\n<li>Stewart claimed that Athens was not a rising power and that the rivals experienced a &ldquo;clash of cultures&rdquo; instead.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to use a quotation to challenge Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict between Athens and Sparta. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c1154794-1106-44bb-871d-6565cb698afc","content":"<p>According to Allison&rsquo;s Thucydides trap theory, whenever &ldquo;a rising power is threatening to displace a ruling power,&rdquo; conflict is likely.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"7c92f05f-ab22-4e85-a613-65952d081391","content":"<p>Thucydides wrote that conflict between the two powers was &ldquo;inevitable,&rdquo; although Stewart later challenged the historical basis of this claim.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"3e3c4f27-c1a4-4a79-ac5a-876af6d55a6c","content":"<p>According to Stewart, a &ldquo;clash of cultures&rdquo; between Athens and Sparta caused the conflict, not Athens&rsquo;s rise.</p>"},{"id":"e1dcce25-1dd1-4a42-9e79-87c5797827da","content":"<p>Thucydides explained that conflict was caused by &ldquo;the rise of Athens and the fear this instilled in Sparta,&rdquo; but Allison disagreed, seeing the conflict as an example of the Thucydides trap.</p>"}],"keys":["3e3c4f27-c1a4-4a79-ac5a-876af6d55a6c"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. Using a quotation from Stewart, the sentence challenges Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation that the rise of Athens caused the conflict, suggesting that it was instead caused by a \"clash of cultures.\"</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the sentence uses a quotation, the quotation doesn&rsquo;t challenge Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict. Choice B is incorrect. While the sentence mentions that Stewart challenged Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict, it doesn&rsquo;t use a quotation to challenge Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation: the quoted word \"inevitable\" is from Thucydides. Choice D is incorrect. While the sentence appears to refute Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation, it does so in a way that misrepresents the information in the notes; Allison&rsquo;s Thucydides trap theory is based on Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation of the conflict. Thus, Allison&rsquo;s theory affirms, rather than challenges, Thucydides&rsquo;s explanation.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669211,"updateDate":1743430669211}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669211, 1743430669211),
    ($SATQ$e876e395$SATQ$, $SATQ$bbc4e5f1-ff38-4b85-a2b3-9bae4f358a79$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>The melting rate of glaciers varies based on air temperature.</li>
<li>In the warm summer months, massive glaciers on the coast of Greenland melt into the surrounding water.</li>
<li>The melting glaciers contribute to rising sea levels each summer.</li>
<li>Huge icebergs also break off Greenland&rsquo;s glaciers into the water and melt.</li>
<li>In 2017, geoscientist Twila Moon found that the iceberg melting rate depends not on air temperature but on water temperature.</li>
<li>Because water temperature is consistent, melting icebergs contribute to rising sea levels all year.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"06c649b4-5832-488f-a7cd-c06f31e9450b","content":"<p>Because icebergs break off Greenland&rsquo;s glaciers into the water, their melting rate depends on water temperature.</p>"},{"id":"0334afd5-cbf7-40e5-929c-5a8d5fa43592","content":"<p>Greenland&rsquo;s glaciers and icebergs both melt during the year, contributing to rising sea levels.</p>"},{"id":"afae18a8-ff59-4f98-bbff-0af2ef1962ac","content":"<p>Geoscientist Twila Moon found that the melting rate of Greenland&rsquo;s icebergs, unlike that of glaciers, does not depend on air temperature.</p>"},{"id":"e005a12a-cdcc-41d0-b3ca-5b319d4b7434","content":"<p>Glaciers on the coast of Greenland melt during the warm summer months into the surrounding water, the temperature of which remains consistent throughout the year.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0334afd5-cbf7-40e5-929c-5a8d5fa43592"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland, noting that both melt and thereby contribute to rising sea levels.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence provides information about the melting rate of icebergs in Greenland; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a difference between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland, noting that their melting rates depend on different factors; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence explains the conditions under which glaciers in Greenland melt; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e876e395","external_id":"bbc4e5f1-ff38-4b85-a2b3-9bae4f358a79","vaultid":null,"uId":"2d221a90-0763-4716-ab04-d4c435932dd7","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The melting rate of glaciers varies based on air temperature.</li>\n<li>In the warm summer months, massive glaciers on the coast of Greenland melt into the surrounding water.</li>\n<li>The melting glaciers contribute to rising sea levels each summer.</li>\n<li>Huge icebergs also break off Greenland&rsquo;s glaciers into the water and melt.</li>\n<li>In 2017, geoscientist Twila Moon found that the iceberg melting rate depends not on air temperature but on water temperature.</li>\n<li>Because water temperature is consistent, melting icebergs contribute to rising sea levels all year.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"06c649b4-5832-488f-a7cd-c06f31e9450b","content":"<p>Because icebergs break off Greenland&rsquo;s glaciers into the water, their melting rate depends on water temperature.</p>"},{"id":"0334afd5-cbf7-40e5-929c-5a8d5fa43592","content":"<p>Greenland&rsquo;s glaciers and icebergs both melt during the year, contributing to rising sea levels.</p>"},{"id":"afae18a8-ff59-4f98-bbff-0af2ef1962ac","content":"<p>Geoscientist Twila Moon found that the melting rate of Greenland&rsquo;s icebergs, unlike that of glaciers, does not depend on air temperature.</p>"},{"id":"e005a12a-cdcc-41d0-b3ca-5b319d4b7434","content":"<p>Glaciers on the coast of Greenland melt during the warm summer months into the surrounding water, the temperature of which remains consistent throughout the year.</p>"}],"keys":["0334afd5-cbf7-40e5-929c-5a8d5fa43592"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The sentence emphasizes a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland, noting that both melt and thereby contribute to rising sea levels.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence provides information about the melting rate of icebergs in Greenland; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland. Choice C is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes a difference between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland, noting that their melting rates depend on different factors; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence explains the conditions under which glaciers in Greenland melt; it doesn&rsquo;t emphasize a similarity between glaciers and icebergs in Greenland.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323047,"updateDate":1730147323047}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323047, 1730147323047),
    ($SATQ$e887dab1$SATQ$, $SATQ$1e891785-8515-4d26-8f9c-4e2497efedcb$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>&ldquo;Organ<sup>2</sup>/<span data-ssml-say-as="characters">ASLSP</span> (As Slow as Possible)&rdquo; is a musical piece by avant-garde composer John Cage.</li>
<li>A specially designed automated organ in <span data-ssml-sub-alias="St">St.</span> Burchardi Church in Halberstadt, Germany, began playing the piece in <span data-ssml-say-as="date">2001</span>.</li>
<li>It is scheduled to stop playing the piece in <span data-ssml-say-as="date">2640</span>.</li>
<li>The performance will last 639 years.</li>
<li>It will be the longest continuous musical performance in history.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to indicate how long John Cage&rsquo;s musical piece will last. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4cfdd5c0-f06a-4b87-b084-3295ac29261d","content":"<p>John Cage is the composer of the musical piece &ldquo;Organ<sup>2</sup>/<span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">ASLSP</span> (As Slow as Possible).&rdquo;</p>"},{"id":"f76b9bfb-afe8-49c6-a630-692190679282","content":"<p>&ldquo;Organ<sup>2</sup>/<span data-ssml-say-as=\"characters\">ASLSP</span> (As Slow as Possible)&rdquo; is a musical piece currently being played in <span data-ssml-sub-alias=\"St\">St.</span> Burchardi Church in Halberstadt, Germany.</p>"},{"id":"07b4a596-f508-4ced-a286-ecefdc0b90a5","content":"<p>Lasting 639 years, John Cage&rsquo;s musical piece will be the longest continuous musical performance in history.</p>"},{"id":"ba3c4157-447d-403e-a72d-0937ebd539cf","content":"<p>An organ in <span data-ssml-sub-alias=\"St\">St.</span> Burchardi Church in Halberstadt, Germany, began playing a musical piece by avant-garde composer John Cage.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["07b4a596-f508-4ced-a286-ecefdc0b90a5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence indicates how long John Cage&rsquo;s musical piece will last, noting that it will last 639 years and be the longest continuous musical performance in history.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence identifies John Cage as the composer and provides the name of the musical piece; it doesn&rsquo;t indicate how long the piece will last. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence provides the name of the musical piece and where it is currently being played; it doesn&rsquo;t indicate how long the piece will last. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence mentions where the musical piece is being played and identifies John Cage as the composer; it doesn&rsquo;t indicate how long the piece will last.</p>$SATQ$, 