nuous musical performance in history.</p>"},{"id":"ba3c4157-447d-403e-a72d-0937ebd539cf","content":"<p>An organ in <span data-ssml-sub-alias=\"St\">St.</span> Burchardi Church in Halberstadt, Germany, began playing a musical piece by avant-garde composer John Cage.</p>"}],"keys":["07b4a596-f508-4ced-a286-ecefdc0b90a5"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence indicates how long John Cage&rsquo;s musical piece will last, noting that it will last 639 years and be the longest continuous musical performance in history.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence identifies John Cage as the composer and provides the name of the musical piece; it doesn&rsquo;t indicate how long the piece will last. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence provides the name of the musical piece and where it is currently being played; it doesn&rsquo;t indicate how long the piece will last. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence mentions where the musical piece is being played and identifies John Cage as the composer; it doesn&rsquo;t indicate how long the piece will last.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771167,"updateDate":1776362771167}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771167, 1776362771167),
    ($SATQ$e965fd73$SATQ$, $SATQ$cab41b8d-25e3-4e64-b68e-a32e802e8376$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$TRA$SATQ$, $SATQ$Transitions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Preston Singletary is a Tlingit glass artist who often collaborates with other artists. <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> he has worked with Tewa pottery artist Jody Naranjo several times. Together, Singletary and Naranjo have created pottery-inspired glass pieces such as <em>Sunset Stampede</em> and <em>Kiva Steps</em>.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d26b63a9-30a9-4e29-acf6-7debe2f72f04","content":"<p>In conclusion,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"d64e4976-6a02-4129-9f8a-8cd837507240","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"b569030e-45e5-45a3-85e6-d65aad58fbfc","content":"<p>However,</p>"},{"id":"683264db-ae0e-44bb-9892-d74132c2ab08","content":"<p>In comparison,&nbsp;</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d64e4976-6a02-4129-9f8a-8cd837507240"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. "For example" logically signals that this sentence&mdash;noting Singletary&rsquo;s work with Jody Naranjo&mdash;provides an example supporting the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because "in conclusion" illogically signals that the information in this sentence concludes or summarizes the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists. Instead, it provides an example in support of that point. Choice C is incorrect because "however" illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists. Instead, it provides an example in support of that point. Choice D is incorrect because "in comparison" illogically signals that the information in this sentence is being compared to the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists. Instead, it provides an example in support of that point.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e965fd73","external_id":"cab41b8d-25e3-4e64-b68e-a32e802e8376","vaultid":null,"uId":"9f4acc22-afd8-4908-ba71-3c5a6275ad72","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"TRA","skill_desc":"Transitions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Preston Singletary is a Tlingit glass artist who often collaborates with other artists. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> he has worked with Tewa pottery artist Jody Naranjo several times. Together, Singletary and Naranjo have created pottery-inspired glass pieces such as <em>Sunset Stampede</em> and <em>Kiva Steps</em>.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d26b63a9-30a9-4e29-acf6-7debe2f72f04","content":"<p>In conclusion,&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"d64e4976-6a02-4129-9f8a-8cd837507240","content":"<p>For example,</p>"},{"id":"b569030e-45e5-45a3-85e6-d65aad58fbfc","content":"<p>However,</p>"},{"id":"683264db-ae0e-44bb-9892-d74132c2ab08","content":"<p>In comparison,&nbsp;</p>"}],"keys":["d64e4976-6a02-4129-9f8a-8cd837507240"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. \"For example\" logically signals that this sentence&mdash;noting Singletary&rsquo;s work with Jody Naranjo&mdash;provides an example supporting the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because \"in conclusion\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence concludes or summarizes the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists. Instead, it provides an example in support of that point. Choice C is incorrect because \"however\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence contrasts with the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists. Instead, it provides an example in support of that point. Choice D is incorrect because \"in comparison\" illogically signals that the information in this sentence is being compared to the previous point about Singletary&rsquo;s collaborations with other artists. Instead, it provides an example in support of that point.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323044,"updateDate":1730147323044}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323044, 1730147323044),
    ($SATQ$e98b1690$SATQ$, $SATQ$122def51-3b7a-48b3-80ed-7c47c5fd5ec5$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Expression of Ideas$SATQ$, $SATQ$EOI$SATQ$, $SATQ$SYN$SATQ$, $SATQ$Rhetorical Synthesis$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bike-share programs provide bicycles for shared use.</li>
<li>In docked bike sharing, riders rent a bike and return it to designated docking stations.</li>
<li>Docked programs are orderly and offer consistency to riders but require significant space and money to implement.</li>
<li>In dockless bike sharing, riders locate a bike and leave it wherever they choose.</li>
<li>Dockless programs are relatively simple and inexpensive to implement and offer flexibility to riders.</li>
<li>Dockless programs can be disorganized.</li>
</ul>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The student wants to compare some disadvantages of docked and dockless bike-share programs. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"85408059-e480-440d-8ab8-836c84ca177c","content":"<p>Dockless programs can be disorganized; docked programs, on the other hand, offer order and consistency.</p>"},{"id":"5f177c53-945d-4c7e-bbf7-d86115ed9400","content":"<p>Worth noting is that while dockless programs are relatively easy and inexpensive to implement, they are less flexible than docked programs.</p>"},{"id":"d71cd4cf-4d33-4410-ba5f-8cebdc2d4fd7","content":"<p>Docked programs are more resource-intensive than dockless programs, but they avoid some of the latter&rsquo;s organizational challenges.</p>"},{"id":"652cca03-a993-4a7c-9338-838c0620917e","content":"<p>Though dockless programs offer flexibility, docked bike-share programs provide bicycles for shared use.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d71cd4cf-4d33-4410-ba5f-8cebdc2d4fd7"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence compares some disadvantages of docked and dockless bike-share programs, explaining that while docked programs are more resource-intensive (requiring significant space and money), dockless programs have greater organizational challenges.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence compares dockless programs to docked programs, noting an advantage of docked programs: they offer order and consistency. It doesn&rsquo;t compare disadvantages of the two types of programs. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence compares dockless programs to docked programs, noting an advantage of dockless programs: they are easy and inexpensive to implement. However, it misrepresents information from the notes, stating that dockless programs are less flexible than docked programs. In addition, it doesn&rsquo;t compare disadvantages of the two types of programs. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes an advantage of dockless programs, then makes a general statement that applies to both types of programs; it doesn&rsquo;t compare disadvantages of the two types of programs.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"e98b1690","external_id":"122def51-3b7a-48b3-80ed-7c47c5fd5ec5","vaultid":null,"uId":"b67ab108-840f-4942-93c5-73df464d6e4c","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"EOI","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill_cd":"SYN","skill_desc":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bike-share programs provide bicycles for shared use.</li>\n<li>In docked bike sharing, riders rent a bike and return it to designated docking stations.</li>\n<li>Docked programs are orderly and offer consistency to riders but require significant space and money to implement.</li>\n<li>In dockless bike sharing, riders locate a bike and leave it wherever they choose.</li>\n<li>Dockless programs are relatively simple and inexpensive to implement and offer flexibility to riders.</li>\n<li>Dockless programs can be disorganized.</li>\n</ul>","stem":"<p>The student wants to compare some disadvantages of docked and dockless bike-share programs. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"85408059-e480-440d-8ab8-836c84ca177c","content":"<p>Dockless programs can be disorganized; docked programs, on the other hand, offer order and consistency.</p>"},{"id":"5f177c53-945d-4c7e-bbf7-d86115ed9400","content":"<p>Worth noting is that while dockless programs are relatively easy and inexpensive to implement, they are less flexible than docked programs.</p>"},{"id":"d71cd4cf-4d33-4410-ba5f-8cebdc2d4fd7","content":"<p>Docked programs are more resource-intensive than dockless programs, but they avoid some of the latter&rsquo;s organizational challenges.</p>"},{"id":"652cca03-a993-4a7c-9338-838c0620917e","content":"<p>Though dockless programs offer flexibility, docked bike-share programs provide bicycles for shared use.</p>"}],"keys":["d71cd4cf-4d33-4410-ba5f-8cebdc2d4fd7"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. The sentence compares some disadvantages of docked and dockless bike-share programs, explaining that while docked programs are more resource-intensive (requiring significant space and money), dockless programs have greater organizational challenges.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The sentence compares dockless programs to docked programs, noting an advantage of docked programs: they offer order and consistency. It doesn&rsquo;t compare disadvantages of the two types of programs. Choice B is incorrect. The sentence compares dockless programs to docked programs, noting an advantage of dockless programs: they are easy and inexpensive to implement. However, it misrepresents information from the notes, stating that dockless programs are less flexible than docked programs. In addition, it doesn&rsquo;t compare disadvantages of the two types of programs. Choice D is incorrect. The sentence emphasizes an advantage of dockless programs, then makes a general statement that applies to both types of programs; it doesn&rsquo;t compare disadvantages of the two types of programs.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669203,"updateDate":1743430669203}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669203, 1743430669203)
